---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalNotice from '../components/LegalNotice.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${site.name} handles personal information, newsletter signups, candidate details and analytics.`}
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { label: 'Privacy Policy' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        How we handle personal information when you use this website, join the
        talent network or subscribe to the newsletter.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container legal-page">
    <LegalNotice />
    {/* TODO: Have this policy reviewed by a qualified Indian legal professional. */}

    <div class="prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {site.legal.lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is an independent marketing and analytics careers brand
        operated in {site.legal.jurisdiction}. In this policy, "we", "us" and
        "our" refer to {site.name}. You can contact us at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What this policy covers</h2>
      <p>
        This policy explains what personal information we collect through this
        website, why we collect it, how it is handled and the choices available
        to you. It applies to this website and to enquiries, newsletter signups,
        talent network applications and employer hiring briefs submitted through
        it.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Information you provide.</strong> Depending on the form you
          use, this may include your name, email address, phone number (optional),
          current role, skills, years of experience, location, expected salary
          range (optional), notice period (optional), LinkedIn URL, company name,
          role details and any message you write.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Newsletter information.</strong> Your email address and any
          preferences you give to our newsletter provider.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical information.</strong> If analytics is enabled, we
          receive aggregated information about page visits, such as the pages
          viewed, approximate region and referring source. We use cookieless,
          privacy-friendly analytics where possible. Analytics is off by default
          and can be checked in the website settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Consent records.</strong> A record of the consent you give when
          you submit a form or subscribe, where we need it.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not ask for payment details through this website, and we do not
        create user accounts.
      </p>

      <h2>4. How we use your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your enquiry or message.</li>
        <li>To consider you for roles and share relevant opportunities, with your agreement.</li>
        <li>To understand an employer's hiring brief and respond to it.</li>
        <li>To send the newsletter you asked for.</li>
        <li>To improve the website, resources and services.</li>
        <li>To keep records and comply with legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Consent and lawful handling</h2>
      <p>
        Where consent is required, we ask for it clearly and you can withdraw it
        at any time. We aim to handle personal information in line with
        applicable Indian law, including the Digital Personal Data Protection Act,
        2023 where it applies, and other laws that may apply to you. This policy
        is a general explanation, not legal advice.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Who we share information with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information. We may share it with:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Service providers</strong> that host this website, process
          forms, send the newsletter or provide analytics. These providers
          process information on our instructions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Employers or their representatives</strong>, but only when you
          have agreed that we can share your details for a specific opportunity.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Professional advisers and authorities</strong> where necessary
          for legal, tax, regulatory or fraud-prevention reasons.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A successor organisation</strong> if the brand or its assets are
          transferred, subject to appropriate safeguards.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not use advertising cookies. If analytics is enabled,
        we use a privacy-friendly provider (Cloudflare Web Analytics or
        Plausible) that is intended to work without cookies. A short notice
        appears on the site when analytics is enabled, and you can dismiss it.
        Your browser settings can also block scripts.
      </p>

      <h2>8. How long we keep information</h2>
      <p>
        We keep personal information only for as long as we need it for the
        purpose it was collected for, or as required by law. Candidate and
        employer details are reviewed periodically. You can ask us to delete
        information you have given us, subject to any legal or record-keeping
        obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect
        personal information. No website, email or storage system is completely
        secure, so we cannot promise absolute security. Please avoid sending
        sensitive information that is not needed for your enquiry.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on the law that applies to you, you may have the right to
        access, correct, update or delete your personal information, withdraw
        consent, object to certain processing, or ask for a copy of the
        information you provided. To make a request, email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We may need to verify
        your identity before acting on a request.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can unsubscribe from the newsletter using the link in every email or
        by contacting us.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Children</h2>
      <p>
        This website is intended for people aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has
        provided information to us, contact us so we can delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>12. International processing</h2>
      <p>
        Our service providers may process information in countries other than
        India. Where that happens, we take reasonable steps to ensure appropriate
        safeguards are in place as required by applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        This website may link to third-party sites, tools or resources. Their
        privacy practices are their own. Read their policies before sharing
        personal information with them.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the brand grows or the law changes. The
        "last updated" date at the top will change when we do. Material changes
        will be described on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Contact and grievances</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions or complaints, contact our grievance contact,
        {site.legal.grievanceContact}, at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Our place of business
        is {site.legal.city}. We will try to resolve concerns promptly.
      </p>
      {/* TODO: Replace the grievance contact and city in src/config/site.ts. */}
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
